// Practice quiz: Compose: the Spring Boot service and its database
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: containers-cicd/containers-and-compose/compose-spring-boot-and-database

::o1 build or image::In compose.yaml, which line makes Compose build the API from the Dockerfile in ./backend? {
~image\: ./backend #Not quite. image names a ready-made image, not a folder.
~context\: backend only, under services #Not quite. context belongs inside a build section.
~FROM ./backend #Not quite. FROM is a Dockerfile instruction, not Compose.
=build\: ./backend #Correct. build points at a folder with a Dockerfile.
}

::o1 keep database data::What keeps PostgreSQL data across container re-creation in compose.yaml? {
~Nothing extra; Compose keeps container files forever #Not quite. Files in a removed container are gone.
~Add restart\: always #Not quite. Restarting keeps a container running; it does not store data elsewhere.
~Publish port 5432 #Not quite. Ports control connections, not storage.
=Mount a named volume at /var/lib/postgresql and declare it under the top-level volumes key #Correct. The named volume outlives the container.
}

::o2 password kept out of compose.yaml::Which compose.yaml line keeps a disposable local database password out of the file? {
~POSTGRES_PASSWORD\: devpass1 #Not quite. The value is then written in the file and committed with it.
=POSTGRES_PASSWORD\: $\{DB_PASSWORD\} #Correct. Compose fills it from the environment or an untracked .env file.
~POSTGRES_PASSWORD\: .env #Not quite. That sets the password to the text .env.
~Leave it out; PostgreSQL needs no password #Not quite. The postgres image requires a password setting to start.
}

::o2 Spring datasource::Which environment variable sets Spring Boot's database URL for the API container? {
~DATABASE_URL #Not quite. Spring Boot does not read that name by default.
~POSTGRES_URL #Not quite. POSTGRES_ variables configure the postgres image, not Spring.
=SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL #Correct. Spring Boot maps upper-case underscore variables to spring.datasource.url.
~spring.datasource.url\=... in compose.yaml under ports #Not quite. Settings go under environment, not ports.
}

::o3 down keeps volumes::After docker compose down, what is left? {
=The named volumes, with their data #Correct. down removes containers and the network but keeps named volumes.
~Nothing at all #Not quite. Only down -v also removes named volumes.
~The running containers #Not quite. down stops and removes them.
~The network only #Not quite. down removes the network too.
}

::o3 list the stack::Which command lists the containers of the current Compose stack and their status? {
=docker compose ps #Correct. It lists the stack's containers with state and ports.
~docker compose down #Not quite. That removes them.
~docker volume ls #Not quite. That lists volumes.
~docker compose up -d #Not quite. That starts the stack.
}
